It is Wednesday.
I go to a café at six o'clock.
Frau Krüger is already waiting at a table.
"Good evening, Frau Flores," she says.
"Good evening, Frau Krüger," I answer.
We drink coffee and talk a lot.
Frau Krüger is very nice.
Then she smiles.
"Shall we say 'du'?" she asks warmly.
"My name is Sabine."
I am very happy.
"I would love to," I answer.
"I am Maya."
"Do you go to the office every day?" asks Sabine.
"Yes, but I do not always take the U-Bahn," I say.
"Now I sometimes ride my bicycle."
Sabine nods and drinks her coffee.
We sit together for another hour.
